<%# The navbar cart: an icon with a live item-count badge, linking to /cart.

    This was a <details> dropdown repeating the item count, the subtotal, a
    "View cart" link and a Checkout control. It was removed because it could not
    do the one thing a checkout entry point now has to do: collect a delivery
    postcode. Shipping is priced into the Stripe line items before Stripe
    collects the address, so checkout is refused without a destination, and a
    panel with no postcode field could only ever send the customer to /cart
    anyway. Two clicks to reach what the icon reaches in one.

    turbo: false because the cart page is a full navigation, matching the
    "View cart" link this replaces.

    Kept inside the turbo_frame so the add-to-cart streams that replace
    "cart_counter" still land, and the badge still updates without a reload. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "cart_counter" do %>
  <%= link_to cart_path, class: "btn btn-ghost btn-sm", "aria-label": "View cart", data: { turbo: false } do %>
    <div class="indicator">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"> <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 3h2l.4 2M7 13h10l4-8H5.4M7 13L5.4 5M7 13l-2.293 2.293c-.63.63-.184 1.707.707 1.707H17m0 0a2 2 0 100 4 2 2 0 000-4zm-8 2a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0z" /> </svg>
      <span class="badge badge-sm indicator-item border-black text-neutral"><%= Current.cart&.line_items_count || 0 %></span>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
